# Publish the release tag

A `@logimaxx/kgrid` version bump is not done until the version commit, the git tag, and the npm package are all published. There is no workflow that publishes on tag push. `./version.sh` pushes the tag and does not run `npm publish`.

This is standing permission to commit and push for a KGrid version bump. Do it in the same task, without asking again.

1. `npm run release` (tests + build). If `dist/` changed, commit that first.
2. `npm version patch|minor|major` (or `./version.sh`), which commits `package.json` and creates the tag.
3. Push the branch and the tag: `git push && git push --tags`.
4. `npm publish`. Confirm `npm view @logimaxx/kgrid@X.Y.Z version`.
5. Only then bump MaxxOps (`consume-in-maxxops.mdc`). Do not point MaxxOps at a version that is not on npm.
